in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @magic
in @magic/contract

# @magic/surface — the gauge-visible interface species.
#
# Tick 12 of the refined /loop discipline. Tick 11's residue: bilateral
# predicates declared at @magic/contract (invariant_preserved) and
# @magic/audit (audited) but no consumer that exercises the discipline.
# This species is the FIRST CONSUMER of the @magic family's bilateral
# predicates via `requires` clauses (Seam C5+ gap closure).
#
# CRQ for tick 12: which species is the first consumer of the @magic
# family's bilateral predicates? Without a consumer, the predicates
# are paint — the same failure mode Seam caught in the decorative
# Spencer-Brown inheritance at tick 11.
#
# Answer: @magic/surface. The surface IS what the observer sees; for
# the surface to be honest, it MUST require the contract bind it to
# a mechanism that preserves the surface-altitude invariants. That
# requirement IS the substrate-pull-correct first `requires` clause
# at @magic altitude.
#
# === The surface as gauge ===
#
# Per recognition #80, the surface IS the gauge-visible interface
# (5-op signature observable from outside the encapsulation). Per
# recognition #79 (NEEDS WORK on op↔axis mapping but still naming
# the gauge basis), the gauge is the 5-op algebra. The surface IS
# the substrate's gauge-side carrier at @magic altitude.
#
# At Clarke's-law altitude (recognition #80): the surface IS what
# the audience sees the magician do. The gauge-visible focus /
# project / split. The matter (sleight, preparation, mechanism) is
# encapsulated behind it.
#
# === The species's load-bearing contribution ===
#
# This species adds:
#
# - `surface_invariant` carrier (substrate-typed invariant the surface
#   commits to upholding).
# - `expose(mechanism) -> magic_surface` action: takes a mechanism and
#   produces its gauge-visible surface. The substrate-pull-correct
#   surface emergence: the matter is encapsulated; the gauge surface
#   is what's exposed.
# - `surface_honest` predicate: bilateral verdict that the surface
#   accurately represents what the mechanism delivers. The FIRST
#   consumer of @magic/contract.invariant_preserved.
#
# The discipline tick 11 named is exercised here: `expose` requires
# `invariant_preserved(c, my_invariant)` via the contract that binds
# this surface to its mechanism. That's the first non-decorative
# `requires` clause in the @magic family.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   gauge field (physics)       Yang-Mills 1954. The original gauge.
#                               @magic/surface IS the gauge-field
#                               carrier at substrate altitude.
#   public interface            Software engineering's
#                               encapsulation discipline (Parnas
#                               1972, "On the Criteria To Be Used
#                               in Decomposing Systems into Modules").
#                               @magic/surface IS the substrate-decl
#                               of "information hiding's revealed
#                               half."
#   stage-magic patter          The magician's verbal accompaniment
#                               to the trick. The gauge-visible
#                               narration that frames what the
#                               audience interprets.
#
# Spec context: docs/math/the-tower/recognition-80-magic-as-form-
#               process-substrate-decl.md.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; surface_honest IS the
#                       alignment check at the gauge altitude),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (surface_invariant
#                       and the action signatures are typed).
# Related shards: magic.mirror (the family-root; magic_surface and
#                  magic_invariant declared here),
#                 magic/contract.mirror (the contract this species
#                  requires; surface_honest consumes
#                  invariant_preserved).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/magic/surface.mirror` declares `@magic/surface` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/physics/yang-mills-1954
source @arxiv/programming/parnas-1972

# === surface_invariant carrier ===
#
# A typed reference per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming a specific
# invariant the surface commits to upholding. Distinct from
# magic_invariant (which lives at family-root and names contract-
# level invariants) by being scoped to surface-altitude commitments:
# what the observer can verify from the gauge alone.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type surface_invariant = ref

# === expose action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary action that produces a magic_surface from
# a mechanism. The substrate-pull-correct surface emergence: the
# matter is encapsulated; the gauge-visible surface is what's exposed.
#
# At Clarke's-law altitude: expose IS the magician's act of presenting
# the trick — the audience sees what the gauge presents; the
# mechanism stays hidden behind it.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
expose(m: magic_mechanism) -> magic_surface { \ }

# === observe action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary action that an external observer takes on
# a surface, producing an observation ref. The observation IS what
# the observer reads from the gauge alone — the matter is opaque.
#
# Per [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]]: the observation
# IS the substrate's gauge-side reading; the mechanism behind the
# surface stays encapsulated.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
observe(s: magic_surface) -> ref { \ }

# === surface_honest action ===
#
# THE FIRST NON-DECORATIVE `requires` CLAUSE CONSUMER per Seam tick
# 11 closure. The substrate-vocabulary action that verifies a surface
# is honest: the contract that binds it to its mechanism preserves
# the surface-altitude invariants.
#
# This is the alignment check at the gauge altitude. Per recognition
# #57: alignment IS the boundary contract enforced at @io; per #80:
# @magic/contract IS what alignment enforces. surface_honest exercises
# the discipline by requiring invariant_preserved(c, inv) on the
# contract that produced this surface.
#
# requires invariant_preserved(c, inv): the substrate-political
# bilateral commitment that the contract honors the named invariant.
# This `requires` clause IS the discipline tick 11's consolidation
# enabled — the predicate declared at @magic/contract finally has
# its first consumer.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
surface_honest(s: magic_surface, c: magic_contract, inv: magic_invariant) -> verdict
requires invariant_preserved(c, inv)
{ \ }

out @magic/surface
out surface_invariant
out expose
out observe
out surface_honest
